# WebBuilder environment template
# Copy to `.env` locally (or set the same keys in the deployment secret
# manager) and fill in real values. NEVER commit a filled-in `.env`.
#
# How this file is organised:
#   [server]   Variables actually read by the Go server (os.Getenv).
#              Only JWT_SECRET is required to start; the rest are optional
#              and degrade gracefully when unset (see the comments).
#   [test-only] Read only by tests, never by the running server.
#   [reserved] Keys kept for compatibility / generated-project templates.
#              The server does NOT read them today — see the notes.
#   [frontend] Variables for generated apps / the Vite frontend, NOT read
#              by the server. They are documented here so generated
#              `.env.example` files stay consistent with this one.
#
# NOT environment variables (do not invent them): SMTP, payment-gateway
# and per-provider OAuth client secrets are stored in the database
# (PlatformSetting, via the admin panel), not in env. The app-database
# PostgreSQL password is read from the `../.pg-password` file, and the
# AI-key encryption key falls back to `$HOME/.webbuilder-key` (mode 600).

# ── [server] Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# JWT signing secret for login tokens. The server refuses to start
# without it (see server/main.go). It may also be provided via the
# `../.jwt-secret` file instead of env; env takes precedence.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=

# ── [server] AI provider (OpenAI-compatible) ───────────────────────
# All three must be set together for AI generation to work; if any is
# missing the AI features report "not configured" instead of starting.
# Per-workspace overrides can also be set from the admin panel (AIConfig).
# Example base URL for an OpenAI-compatible gateway:
AI_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=

# ── [server] Public URL & OAuth ────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL used to build OAuth redirect URIs. Defaults in code to
# https://build.clipku.my.id when unset.
PUBLIC_URL=https://build.clipku.my.id
# OAuth client IDs (public identifiers only). The matching client
# secrets are NOT read from env — the Google/GitHub callback handlers
# are currently stubs and the OAuth secrets live in the database
# (oauth_<provider>_client_id / oauth_<provider>_client_secret).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=

# ── [server] AI-key encryption ─────────────────────────────────────
# Base64 of a 32-byte AES-256-GCM key, used to encrypt AI provider keys
# at rest. Optional: if unset and `$HOME/.webbuilder-key` does not exist,
# the server generates and stores one there (mode 600). If set but not
# valid base64 of exactly 32 bytes, it is ignored and a fresh key is
# generated instead — so set it correctly or leave it empty.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
WEBBUILDER_KEY=

# ── [server] Custom-domain SSL (optional) ──────────────────────────
# All three must be set for automatic SSL issuance on custom domains
# (certbot over SSH on the VPS). VPS_SSH_KEY is either the path to a
# private-key file or the key contents themselves. If any is missing,
# the SSL endpoint returns "not configured" instead of failing.
VPS_SSH_HOST=
VPS_SSH_USER=
VPS_SSH_KEY=

# ── [server] Database (optional) ───────────────────────────────────
# Empty (default) -> SQLite at ../data/webbuilder.db, schema via
# AutoMigrate — the historical behaviour, unchanged.
# postgres://... (or postgresql://...) -> PostgreSQL, schema via
# versioned goose migrations (server/migrations), NOT AutoMigrate.
# sqlite://<path> or file:<path> -> SQLite at that path.
# Any other value is rejected with an error at startup (the server
# refuses to guess). See server/internal/database/database.go.
DATABASE_URL=

# ── [server] Agent queue (optional) ──────────────────────────────────
# Backend job agent: "db" (default, durable — tabel queue_jobs di DB yang
# sama) atau "inprocess" (fallback eksplisit, job hilang saat restart).
# Nilai lain -> server gagal-start. Bila "db" gagal init (mis. tabel
# queue_jobs belum ada di Postgres), server gagal-start TANPA fallback
# diam-diam ke in-memory. Lihat docs/queue.md.
WEBBUILDER_QUEUE=db
# Jumlah consumer paralel yang menjalankan job agent (default 2, 1..8).
WEBBUILDER_QUEUE_WORKERS=2

# ── [server] Tenant execution (optional, default OFF) ──────────────
# Tenant code execution stays disabled unless this is exactly "1".
# Any other value (including "true") keeps it off. Limits below only
# matter when execution is enabled; invalid values fall back to the
# defaults silently. See server/internal/runtime/config.go.
WEBBUILDER_ENABLE_TENANT_EXEC=
# Timeout per tenant execution, in seconds (default 60).
WEBBUILDER_TENANT_EXEC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# Max stdout+stderr bytes kept per execution (default 1048576 = 1 MiB);
# excess output is truncated, not an error.
WEBBUILDER_TENANT_EXEC_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES=1048576

# ── [server] Browser tools (optional, default OFF) ─────────────────
# Agent browser tools (chrome-devtools-mcp + Chrome headless, Fase 1:
# hanya browser_list_console_messages). Hanya "1" yang menyalakan, dan
# browser tools HANYA aktif bila WEBBUILDER_ENABLE_TENANT_EXEC=1 juga
# nyala — keduanya wajib. Bila flag nyala tapi Chrome/MCP tidak tersedia,
# server log error jelas dan agent jalan TANPA alat browser (fail-closed).
# Lihat docs/mcp-browser-integration-plan.md dan docs/isolation.md.
WEBBUILDER_ENABLE_BROWSER_TOOLS=
# Command server MCP (default: npx -y chrome-devtools-mcp@1.13.0 —
# versi di-pin hasil spike Fase 0; jangan @latest supaya reproduksibel).
CHROME_DEVTOOLS_MCP_CMD=
# Path biner Chrome for Testing (default: auto-detect oleh server MCP).
# Contoh VM ini: /home/hatch/workspace/chrome/linux-157.0.8103.78/chrome-linux64/chrome
CHROME_FOR_TESTING_PATH=

# ── [test-only] Not read by the server ─────────────────────────────
# Full postgres:// URL used ONLY by live-Postgres tests
# (server/internal/database/database_test.go, server/internal/queue/db_test.go).
# The tests skip themselves when it is unset. Never set it in production.
WB_TEST_POSTGRES_URL=

# ── [reserved] NOT read by the server today ────────────────────────
# PORT: dibaca server/main.go sebagai port listen (default 18082) dan
# dipakai target proxy /api vite.config hasil scaffold (lihat
# server/internal/handler/runtime.go: serverPort). Bila PORT diubah,
# preview proyek ikut memakai port baru.
PORT=18082

# ── [frontend] Generated apps / Vite (NOT read by the server) ──────
# These are emitted into generated projects' .env.example / .env.local
# by the server (see server/internal/handler/contract.go and runtime.go)
# and are the only VITE_* keys the codebase knows. Never put secrets in
# VITE_* values — they are exposed to the browser.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:18082
VITE_APP_NAME=WebBuilder App
